## Parent Delivery Stack

This feature is a review-feedback child of a parent that delivers as a stack of layered pull requests — one branch and pull request per layer below. The highest position is the top layer.

{{ $top := 0 }}{{ range .Stack }}{{ if gt .Position $top }}{{ $top = .Position }}{{ end }}{{ end }}{{ range .Stack }}- Layer {{ .Position }}{{ if .Title }}: {{ .Title }}{{ end }}{{ if eq .Position $top }} (top layer){{ end }} — phases {{ .Phases }}{{ if .Branch }}, branch {{ .Branch }}{{ end }}
{{ end }}
The default target layer for a review comment's fix is the layer of the pull request that comment was left on. When a fix changes files that belong to a lower stack layer, write an optional fix manifest at {{ .FixManifestPath }} naming the owning layer for every such changed file:

```yaml
entries:
  - layer: 1
    repository: <repository name>
    paths:
      - <repository-relative path>
```

Files not listed in the manifest follow that same default: they land on the layer of the pull request the comment was left on. The manifest is optional — write it only when a fix actually changes lower-layer files. You never run git write commands (commit, push, branch, rebase); the harness owns them.

